WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/feedback/AlertBanner.tsx — a presentational, page-level inline notification:
    AlertBanner({ variant, title?, children, onClose?, icon? }) renders a tinted, backdrop-blurred,
    bordered box (flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border p-4 backdrop-blur-sm) with an optional leading
    icon (titleText tint), an optional emphasised title line (text-sm font-medium, titleText tint), the
    required message line (children; text-xs, text/80 muted tint; mt-0.5 only when a title is present), and
    an optional trailing dismiss (X) button (onClose). `alertVariantMap` keys border-X/20 · bg-X/5 · text-X/80
    · titleText text-X off the union 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger'. The component is "anonymous":
    it has NO t() calls — the caller supplies the strings (prompt "Titles / labels / i18n keys: none extracted").
  Documented data sources / consumers (from the AlertBanner doc comment, read verbatim):
    • useMutationToast (web/src/api/hooks/_toastHelpers.ts) — success(key,fallback) shows one line; error(err,
      key,fallback) shows the translated title PLUS err.message as a secondary line.
    • LiveStaleDataBanner (components/feedback/LiveStaleDataBanner.tsx) — <AlertBanner variant="warning"
      icon=WifiOff title=t('live.staleBanner.title') >t('live.staleBanner.message')</> when the live pipe has
      been disconnected ≥ 2 minutes.
    • OfflineBanner (components/feedback/OfflineBanner.tsx) — <AlertBanner variant="warning" icon=WifiOff
      title=t('pwa.offline.title') >t('pwa.offline.banner')</> while the browser is offline (cached data shown).
  These are THE data the prompt's "Data sources: useMutationToast" + the required loading/empty/error/stale/
  offline states map onto.

SCOPE / ARCHITECTURE NOTE  (no silent drift — disclosed in full)
  The ATOMIC banner primitive already exists: Sources/Components/Feedback/Banners.swift `TSAlertBanner`
  ("Base banner (web AlertBanner)") + its named presets (TSOfflineBanner, TSLiveStaleDataBanner, …). That
  atomic component is OUT OF SCOPE here (prompt "Out of Scope: Atomic shared components (covered by the P4
  component-library bundle prompt)"). This 0113 SHARED SURFACE is therefore the higher-level, DATA-BOUND,
  multi-state AlertBanner HOST — it binds the mutation-toast bus + the live-connection axis (P1/S8), renders
  every state, resolves chrome via the P1/S10 facade, uses the P1/S9 tokens, and emits the P1/S11 view.opened
  telemetry. It reproduces the web AlertBanner composition as scoped subviews (variant-tinted title AND
  message; facade-resolved strings via Text(verbatim:)) rather than calling TSAlertBanner, for two parity
  reasons: (a) the web tints BOTH the title and the message with the variant colour, where TSAlertBanner uses
  neutral text; and (b) the P1/S10 facade resolves to String, incompatible with TSAlertBanner's
  LocalizedStringKey API. Same established precedent as AiLimitBanner (0025) reproducing the web AlertBanner
  body as scoped subviews. The full web AlertBanner API (all four variants + optional icon + optional title +
  message + onClose) is modelled by AlertBannerNotice; AlertBannerNotice.from(mutation:) bridges
  useMutationToast and AlertBannerNotice.connectivity(for:) bridges the OfflineBanner / LiveStaleDataBanner
  consumers verbatim.

